{"step_index":43,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T08:08:37Z","input_tokens":9573,"cache_read_tokens":113184,"output_tokens":8649,"thinking":"The initial scalar value, 1.00, resulted in a lap time very close to the target, differing by only 0.10 seconds. This suggests that the `brentq` algorithm, while calibrating the scalar, effectively converged on the expected lap time of 53.3333 seconds.\n\n\nThe current scalar value of 0.9970 yields a race pitch that exceeds the target range; minor adjustments to the Raidillon geometry are being considered to refine this. Modifying the quintic Z core to `0.193 .. 0.278` brings the maximum race pitch to +13.55° and minimum to -14.45°, within the desired range.\n\n\nInitial suspicion was that the hairpin radius was too tight, but the minimum race radius is less than the constraint. Adjusting the arc width and gentle camber on the Harbor Hairpin resulted in the minimum speed precisely matching the specified deceleration. The hairpin adjustment also has the potential to introduce high speed aero variation.\n\n\nThe negative `off` value at the right-hand hairpin indicates the racing line hugs the inner apex. The calculated race radius being less than the constraint radius suggests the path favors arc length minimization rather than curvature minimization. This explains why the racing line is shorter than the centerline path. A shortest-path strategy is being used instead of a minimum-curvature approach.\n\n\nThe racing line curvature formula highlights a fundamental issue: minimizing arc length, with the current Laplacian constraint, forces the racing line to hug the inner kerb, resulting in a tighter radius than the centerline. The curvature difference between the racing line and the centerline is directly proportional to the second derivative of the offset. To achieve a racing line with a consistently larger radius than the centerline (`R_race > R_cl`), the constraint must be altered to drive the second derivative of the offset in the opposite direction.\n\n\nConsidering how the offset affects racing line curvature, the goal is to reduce curvature magnitude by influencing the second derivative of the offset. Specifically, at a right-hand turn, a positive second derivative will decrease the racing line's curvature magnitude, increasing the radius. Conversely, at a left-hand turn, a negative second derivative achieves the same effect.\n\nThis suggests that an optimization problem must be solved to minimize the integral of a curvature-related term, subject to offset bounds, using either projected L-BFGS-B or biharmonic relaxation; L-BFGS-B computation takes 0.08 seconds for 1850 points with the exact analytic gradient.\n\n\nThe L-BFGS-B algorithm, minimizing curvature, demonstrates an intriguing racing line behavior. Before right turns, the car naturally moves to the left edge, clips the right apex, and tracks out to the left exit. It automatically finds optimal transitions between linked S-bends and settles near a clean racing line on straights with zero curvature spikes. Every corner's racing radius is wider and smoother than the centerline.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\nimport math, time\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import root, brentq, minimize\nfrom scipy.interpolate import CubicSpline\n\nt0 = time.time()\n\ndef smooth_bump(u, u0, u1, edge_frac=0.35):\n    w = (u1 - u0) % 1.0\n    du = (u - u0) % 1.0\n    out = np.zeros_like(u, dtype=float)\n    e = max(1e-6, min(0.499, edge_frac)) * w\n    m_rise = (du > 0.0) & (du < e)\n    x = du[m_rise] / e\n    out[m_rise] = x**3 * (10.0 - 15.0 * x + 6.0 * x * x)\n    m_flat = (du >= e) & (du <= w - e)\n    out[m_flat] = 1.0\n    m_fall = (du > w - e) & (du < w)\n    x = (w - du[m_fall]) / e\n    out[m_fall] = x**3 * (10.0 - 15.0 * x + 6.0 * x * x)\n    return out\n\ndef smooth_step_quintic(x):\n    x = np.clip(x, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return x**3 * (10.0 - 15.0 * x + 6.0 * x * x)\n\ndef corner_turn(u, u0, u1, angle_deg, edge_frac=0.35):\n    b = smooth_bump(u, u0, u1, edge_frac=edge_frac)\n    integ = np.sum(b) / len(u)\n    return b * (math.radians(angle_deg) / max(integ, 1e-12))\n\nM = 12000\nu = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, M, endpoint=False)\ndu = 1.0 / M\n\ndef build_xy_unit(params):\n    a_raid, a_bk, a_hp = params\n    corners = [\n        # Zone 1: canyon_grid (0.00 .. 0.16)\n        (0.098, 0.123, -82.0, 0.34),   # Tight Canyon Chicane Right\n        (0.123, 0.149, +78.0, 0.34),   # Tight Canyon Chicane Left\n        # Zone 2: eau_rouge_climb (0.16 .. 0.33)\n        (0.164, 0.198, +42.0, 0.40),   # Eau-Rouge bottom compression Left\n        (0.198, 0.286, a_raid, 0.38),  # Raidillon sweeping uphill Right\n        (0.286, 0.325, +34.0, 0.40),   # Blind crest Left sweep onto Sky-Bridge (~265 km/h crest -> accelerates on bridge!)\n        # Zone 3: sky_bridge (0.33 .. 0.50)\n        (0.395, 0.445, a_bk,  0.42),   # Fast Sky-Bridge aero kink\n        # Zone 4: banked_bowl_plunge (0.50 .. 0.70)\n        (0.502, 0.576, -188.0, 0.26),  # Sweeping 188-deg Right-Hand Carousel Bowl!\n        (0.598, 0.628, +92.0, 0.34),   # Laguna-Seca Corkscrew tight blind Left drop!\n        (0.630, 0.668, -54.0, 0.36),   # Corkscrew Right sweep toward tunnel!\n        # Zone 5: strobe_tunnel_harbor (0.70 .. 1.00)\n        (0.715, 0.845, +12.0, 0.46),   # Gentle flat-out Cyber-Strobe Tunnel curve\n        (0.854, 0.878, +18.0, 0.42),   # Blinding exit cliffside sweep before heavy braking\n        (0.898, 0.916, a_hp,  0.26),   # Heavy-Braking Cliffside Harbor Hairpin (target ~82 km/h!)\n        (0.946, 0.984, -34.0, 0.45),   # Fast Harbor Waterfront bend onto Finish Straight\n    ]\n    kap = np.zeros_like(u)\n    for u0, u1, ang, ef in corners:\n        kap += corner_turn(u, u0, u1, ang, ef)\n\n    theta = np.cumsum(kap) * du\n    theta -= theta[0]\n    total_dtheta = np.sum(kap) * du\n    cx = np.sum(np.cos(theta)) * du\n    cy = np.sum(np.sin(theta)) * du\n    return kap, theta, np.array([total_dtheta + 2.0 * math.pi, cx, cy])\n\nsol = root(lambda p: build_xy_unit(p)[2], x0=[-175.0, 25.0, -120.0], method='hybr', tol=1e-12)\nprint(\"Solver success:\", sol.success, \"params (deg):\", sol.x)\n\nkap_u, theta_u, _ = build_xy_unit(sol.x)\nx_u = np.cumsum(np.cos(theta_u)) * du\ny_u = np.cumsum(np.sin(theta_u)) * du\nx_u -= x_u[0]\ny_u -= y_u[0]\n\ndef build_z_profile(u):\n    z = np.full_like(u, 0.8)\n    z += 2.2 * smooth_step_quintic((u - 0.05) / (0.16 - 0.05))\n    # Eau-Rouge climb: Z = 3.0 -> +42.0m, tuned so pitch peaks cleanly at +13.3 deg (inside 12.5..14.0)\n    z += 5.0 * smooth_step_quintic((u - 0.160) / (0.326 - 0.160))\n    z += 34.0 * smooth_step_quintic((u - 0.193) / (0.278 - 0.193))\n    # Sky-Bridge crown (+42.0 -> +42.35 -> +42.0m)\n    z += 0.35 * np.sin(np.pi * np.clip((u - 0.33) / 0.17, 0.0, 1.0))**2\n    # Bowl rim + Corkscrew plunge: Z = +42.0 -> +1.5m, tuned so pitch reaches -14.2 deg (inside -13.5..-15.0)\n    z -= 4.3 * smooth_step_quintic((u - 0.525) / (0.696 - 0.525))\n    z -= 36.2 * smooth_step_quintic((u - 0.600) / (0.679 - 0.600))\n    # Tunnel (1.5m) -> Finish (0.8m)\n    z -= 0.7 * smooth_step_quintic((u - 0.860) / (0.975 - 0.860))\n    return z\n\nZ_raw = build_z_profile(u)\n\nTARGET_N = 1850\nTARGET_L3D = TARGET_N * 2.0  # 3700.0 m\n\ndef calc_l3d(L2D):\n    X = np.append(x_u * L2D, x_u[0] * L2D)\n    Y = np.append(y_u * L2D, y_u[0] * L2D)\n    Z = np.append(Z_raw, Z_raw[0])\n    return float(np.sum(np.sqrt(np.diff(X)**2 + np.diff(Y)**2 + np.diff(Z)**2)))\n\nL2D_opt = brentq(lambda L: calc_l3d(L) - TARGET_L3D, 3400.0, 3800.0, xtol=1e-10)\nX_dense = np.append(x_u * L2D_opt, x_u[0] * L2D_opt)\nY_dense = np.append(y_u * L2D_opt, y_u[0] * L2D_opt)\nZ_dense = np.append(Z_raw, Z_raw[0])\nds_dense = np.sqrt(np.diff(X_dense)**2 + np.diff(Y_dense)**2 + np.diff(Z_dense)**2)\ns_dense = np.concatenate([[0.0], np.cumsum(ds_dense)])\ns_dense[-1] = TARGET_L3D\n\ncs_x = CubicSpline(s_dense, X_dense, bc_type='periodic')\ncs_y = CubicSpline(s_dense, Y_dense, bc_type='periodic')\ncs_z = CubicSpline(s_dense, Z_dense, bc_type='periodic')\n\ns_grid = np.arange(TARGET_N, dtype=float) * 2.0\nsf = s_grid / TARGET_L3D\nX = cs_x(s_grid)\nY = cs_y(s_grid)\nZ = cs_z(s_grid)\n\ndx = cs_x(s_grid, 1)\ndy = cs_y(s_grid, 1)\ndz = cs_z(s_grid, 1)\ndxy = np.hypot(dx, dy)\npitch_cl = np.degrees(np.arctan2(dz, dxy))\nddx = cs_x(s_grid, 2)\nddy = cs_y(s_grid, 2)\nkap_cl = (dx * ddy - dy * ddx) / np.maximum(dxy**3, 1e-12)\n\nbank_deg = (\n    +17.4 * smooth_bump(sf, 0.498, 0.580, edge_frac=0.30)\n    - 4.0 * smooth_bump(sf, 0.162, 0.200, edge_frac=0.42)\n    + 5.8 * smooth_bump(sf, 0.198, 0.288, edge_frac=0.40)\n    - 5.5 * smooth_bump(sf, 0.598, 0.630, edge_frac=0.38)\n    + 4.5 * smooth_bump(sf, 0.630, 0.670, edge_frac=0.40)\n    + 2.8 * smooth_bump(sf, 0.895, 0.918, edge_frac=0.38)\n)\n\n# TRUE Minimum-Curvature Optimal Racing Line via L-BFGS-B!\n# Exact linearized racing curvature: k_race(i) = kap_cl(i) / (1 - kap_cl(i)*off(i)) + off''(i)\n# Objective: sum( k_eff^2 + w_d1 * (off')^2 + w_d3 * (off''')^2 + w_c * off^2 )\nds0 = 2.0\nw_d1 = 1.2e-5\nw_d3 = 8.0e-2\nw_c  = 1.5e-8\n\ndef race_obj_and_grad(off):\n    om1 = np.roll(off, 1)\n    op1 = np.roll(off, -1)\n    om2 = np.roll(off, 2)\n    op2 = np.roll(off, -2)\n\n    d2 = (op1 - 2.0 * off + om1) / (ds0 * ds0)\n    d1 = (op1 - om1) / (2.0 * ds0)\n    # 3rd derivative for jerk-free steering smoothness:\n    d3 = (op2 - 2.0 * op1 + 2.0 * om1 - om2) / (2.0 * ds0**3)\n\n    # Include (1 + kap_cl * off) denominator approximation linearly: k_eff = kap_cl * (1 + kap_cl * off) + d2\n    c1 = 1.0 + kap_cl * off\n    keff = kap_cl * c1 + d2\n\n    loss = 0.5 * np.sum(keff**2 + w_d1 * d1**2 + w_d3 * d3**2 + w_c * off**2)\n\n    # Exact adjoint gradient!\n    g_keff = keff\n    grad = g_keff * (kap_cl * kap_cl) + (np.roll(g_keff, 1) - 2.0 * g_keff + np.roll(g_keff, -1)) / (ds0 * ds0)\n    g_d1 = w_d1 * d1\n    grad += (np.roll(g_d1, 1) - np.roll(g_d1, -1)) / (2.0 * ds0)\n    g_d3 = w_d3 * d3\n    grad += (np.roll(g_d3, 2) - 2.0 * np.roll(g_d3, 1) + 2.0 * np.roll(g_d3, -1) - np.roll(g_d3, -2)) / (2.0 * ds0**3)\n    grad += w_c * off\n    return float(loss), grad\n\nres_opt = minimize(\n    race_obj_and_grad,\n    np.zeros(TARGET_N),\n    jac=True,\n    method='L-BFGS-B',\n    bounds=[(-5.10, 5.10)] * TARGET_N,\n    options={'maxiter': 600, 'ftol': 1e-12, 'gtol': 1e-9}\n)\noff = res_opt.x\n# Tiny Gaussian polish (sigma = 2.5 pts = 5m) so bound active-set transitions are C^infty smooth!\nkh = 12\nkx = np.arange(-kh, kh + 1, dtype=float)\nkw = np.exp(-0.5 * (kx / 2.5)**2)\nkw /= kw.sum()\noff = np.convolve(np.concatenate([off[-kh:], off, off[:kh]]), kw, mode='valid')\noff = np.clip(off, -5.2, 5.2)\n\nprint(f\"L-BFGS-B racing line converged in {res_opt.nit} iters ({time.time()-t0:.2f}s), off: [{off.min():.2f}, {off.max():.2f}] m\")\n\ncl_h = np.arctan2(dy, dx)\nh_rad = cl_h.copy()\npt_rad = np.radians(pitch_cl).copy()\nbk_rad = np.radians(bank_deg)\ns_ext = np.append(s_grid, TARGET_L3D)\n\nfor _ in range(6):\n    R0_x, R0_y, R0_z = np.sin(h_rad), -np.cos(h_rad), np.zeros_like(h_rad)\n    U0_x = -np.sin(pt_rad) * np.cos(h_rad)\n    U0_y = -np.sin(pt_rad) * np.sin(h_rad)\n    U0_z = np.cos(pt_rad)\n    Rx = np.cos(bk_rad) * R0_x - np.sin(bk_rad) * U0_x\n    Ry = np.cos(bk_rad) * R0_y - np.sin(bk_rad) * U0_y\n    Rz = np.cos(bk_rad) * R0_z - np.sin(bk_rad) * U0_z\n    RX = X - off * Rx\n    RY = Y - off * Ry\n    RZ = Z - off * Rz\n    cs_rx = CubicSpline(s_ext, np.append(RX, RX[0]), bc_type='periodic')\n    cs_ry = CubicSpline(s_ext, np.append(RY, RY[0]), bc_type='periodic')\n    cs_rz = CubicSpline(s_ext, np.append(RZ, RZ[0]), bc_type='periodic')\n    drx = cs_rx(s_grid, 1)\n    dry = cs_ry(s_grid, 1)\n    drz = cs_rz(s_grid, 1)\n    drxy = np.hypot(drx, dry)\n    h_rad = np.arctan2(dry, drx)\n    pt_rad = np.arctan2(drz, drxy)\n\nddrx = cs_rx(s_grid, 2)\nddry = cs_ry(s_grid, 2)\ncurv_race = (drx * ddry - dry * ddrx) / np.maximum(drxy**3, 1e-12)\n\nprint(f\"Max |kap_cl|: {np.abs(kap_cl).max():.5f} (min R_cl = {1.0/np.abs(kap_cl).max():.2f} m)\")\nprint(f\"Max |curv_race|: {np.abs(curv_race).max():.5f} (min R_race = {1.0/np.abs(curv_race).max():.2f} m)\")\nprint(f\"Max |d(curv_race)| step: {np.abs(np.diff(np.append(curv_race, curv_race[0]))).max():.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Race pitch range: [{np.degrees(pt_rad).min():.2f}, {np.degrees(pt_rad).max():.2f}] deg\")\n\nfor thresh in (120.0, 140.0):\n    min_sep = 1e9\n    for i in range(0, TARGET_N, 2):\n        ds_cyc = np.minimum((s_grid - s_grid[i]) % TARGET_L3D, (s_grid[i] - s_grid) % TARGET_L3D)\n        dist_xy = np.hypot(X - X[i], Y - Y[i])\n        m = dist_xy[ds_cyc >= thresh]\n        if len(m) and m.min() < min_sep:\n            min_sep = float(m.min())\n    print(f\"Min XY sep (|ds| >= {thresh:.0f}m): {min_sep:.2f} m\")\n\nRX_ext = np.append(RX, RX[0])\nRY_ext = np.append(RY, RY[0])\nRZ_ext = np.append(RZ, RZ[0])\nds_race = np.sqrt(np.diff(RX_ext)**2 + np.diff(RY_ext)**2 + np.diff(RZ_ext)**2)\n\ndef solve_lap(scalar):\n    tun_boost = smooth_bump(sf, 0.705, 0.875, edge_frac=0.20)\n    vmax_arr = (91.8 + 3.4 * tun_boost) * math.sqrt(scalar)\n    vmax_arr = np.clip(vmax_arr, 88.0, 95.3)\n\n    a0_lat = 16.5 * scalar\n    c_lat = 0.0075 * scalar\n    bank_term = 9.81 * np.tan(np.abs(bk_rad)) * scalar\n\n    k_abs = np.abs(curv_race)\n    V = np.empty(TARGET_N)\n    for i in range(TARGET_N):\n        denom = k_abs[i] - c_lat\n        if denom <= 1e-6:\n            V[i] = vmax_arr[i]\n        else:\n            V[i] = min(vmax_arr[i], math.sqrt((a0_lat + bank_term[i]) / denom))\n\n    sin_pt = np.sin(pt_rad)\n    for _ in range(8):\n        for i in range(TARGET_N - 1, -1, -1):\n            vn = V[(i + 1) % TARGET_N]\n            ds = ds_race[i]\n            vi = vn\n            for _ in range(3):\n                vm = 0.5 * (vi + vn)\n                abrk = scalar * min(56.0, 21.0 + 0.0052 * vm * vm) + 9.81 * sin_pt[i]\n                abrk = max(5.0, abrk)\n                vi = math.sqrt(vn * vn + 2.0 * abrk * ds)\n            if vi < V[i]:\n                V[i] = vi\n        for i in range(TARGET_N):\n            vp = V[i]\n            ds = ds_race[i]\n            p_pow = (980.0 + 220.0 * tun_boost[i]) * scalar\n            a_tr = scalar * 16.2\n            aacc = min(a_tr, p_pow / max(vp, 12.0)) - 9.81 * sin_pt[i]\n            aacc = max(0.5, aacc)\n            vn_max = min(vmax_arr[(i + 1) % TARGET_N], math.sqrt(vp * vp + 2.0 * aacc * ds))\n            if vn_max < V[(i + 1) % TARGET_N]:\n                V[(i + 1) % TARGET_N] = vn_max\n\n    dt = ds_race / np.maximum(0.5 * (V + np.roll(V, -1)), 1.0)\n    return float(np.sum(dt)), V, dt\n\nTARGET_LAP_S = 96.0 * 60.0 / 108.0  # 53.333333 s\nsc_opt = brentq(lambda s: solve_lap(s)[0] - TARGET_LAP_S, 0.70, 1.30, xtol=1e-9)\nt_lap, V_opt, dt_opt = solve_lap(sc_opt)\nprint(f\"Calibrated scalar = {sc_opt:.5f} -> sim_lap_s = {t_lap:.6f} s (target {TARGET_LAP_S:.6f} s)\")\nprint(f\"Speed range: [{V_opt.min()*3.6:.1f}, {V_opt.max()*3.6:.1f}] km/h ({V_opt.min():.2f} .. {V_opt.max():.2f} m/s)\")\nfor zname, a, b in [\n    (\"canyon_grid\", 0.00, 0.16),\n    (\"eau_rouge_climb\", 0.16, 0.33),\n    (\"sky_bridge\", 0.33, 0.50),\n    (\"banked_bowl_plunge\", 0.50, 0.70),\n    (\"strobe_tunnel_harbor\", 0.70, 1.00),\n]:\n    m = (sf >= a) & (sf < b)\n    print(f\"  {zname:22s}: v=[{V_opt[m].min()*3.6:5.1f}, {V_opt[m].max()*3.6:5.1f}] km/h, Z=[{Z[m].min():5.1f}, {Z[m].max():5.1f}] m, pitch=[{np.degrees(pt_rad[m]).min():6.2f}, {np.degrees(pt_rad[m]).max():6.2f}], bank=[{bank_deg[m].min():5.1f}, {bank_deg[m].max():5.1f}]\")\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\62527b59-0213-41b2-b3ab-ff115c915c3b\\scratch\\design_circuit.py"}},{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python \"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\62527b59-0213-41b2-b3ab-ff115c915c3b\\scratch\\design_circuit.py\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":8000,"toolSummary":"Test L-BFGS-B minimum-curvature racing line and lap calibration"}}]}
